course: dictionary
lesson: 14521
title: Words of danger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Peril is a noun. It means great danger, or something that is a risk. «The kitten was in peril on the busy road.» The words busy road tell you the kitten was in danger, so peril must mean danger.
explain: Stories use peril a lot. «Mole was in peril in the Wild Wood, where the snow was deep and the night was dark.» Here the snow and the dark show the danger. Look for words like dark, storm, cliff or lost near peril, and they will guide you.
explain: Peril has some set phrases. «In peril» means in danger. «At your peril» means at your own risk, so you must be careful. «The perils of the sea» means the dangers of the sea.
explain: To check your meaning, swap danger into the sentence. If «The climbers were in danger on the icy mountain» still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Peril means great danger, or something that is a risk.
fact: «In peril» means in danger, as in «The sailors were in peril in the storm».
fact: «At your peril» means at your own risk, so you must be careful.
fact: «The perils of the sea» means the dangers that sailors face on the sea.
fact: Peril can be countable (a peril, perils) or uncountable, so you can say «There is great peril» or «The perils were many».
exercise: «The climbers were in peril on the icy mountain.» What does in peril mean? | Very cold and wet, but safe | Having a long rest | *In great danger | Far from home
exercise: «Mole knew the Wild Wood held many perils in the snow.» What is a peril here? | A friendly animal | *A danger or risk | A kind of warm coat | A quiet place to sleep
exercise: «Swim past the flags at your peril.» What does at your peril mean? | With your best friends | With a lot of fun | *At your own risk | Very slowly
test: «The sailors spoke of the perils of the open sea.» What are perils here? | Fish and birds | Stories about kings | *Dangers and risks | Warm winds
test: Which word means great danger? | Pencil | *Peril | Puzzle | Pleasure
exam: «Quick, the children are in peril!» What does in peril mean? | They are safe and happy | They are lost in a shop | *They are in great danger | They are tired after school
